urchesne</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Ganz</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Norcia</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name></person-group><year>1981</year><article-title>Event-related brain potentials to human faces in infants.</article-title><source>Child Dev</source><volume>52</volume><fpage>804</fpage><lpage>811</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7285651</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002389-Nelson1"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nelson</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name></person-group><year>1994</year><article-title>Neural correlates of recognition memory in the first postnatal year of life.</article-title><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Dawson</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Fischer</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><source>Human Behavior and the Developing Brain</source><publisher-loc>New York</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Guilford Press</publisher-name><fpage>269</fpage><lpage>313</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002389-Richards1"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Richards</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Attention affects the recognition of briefly presented visual stimuli in infants: An ERP study.</article-title><source>Dev Sci</source><volume>6</volume><fpage>312</fpage><lpage>328</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16718304</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002389-Nelson2"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nelson</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>de Haan</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Neural Correlates of Infants' Visual Responsiveness to Facial Expressions of Emotion.</article-title><source>Dev Psychobiol</source><volume>29(7)</volume><fpage>577</fpage><lpage>595</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8911773</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002389-Grossmann1"><label>25</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Grossmann</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Striano</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Friederici</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Developmental Changes in Infants' Processing of Happy and Angry Facial Expressions: A Neurobehavioral Study.</article-title><source>Brain Cogn</source><volume>64</volume><fpage>30</fpage><lpage>41</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17169471</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002389-Grossmann2"><label>26</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Grossmann</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Striano</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Friederici</surname><given-names>AD</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Infants' electric brain responses to emotional prosody.</article-title><source>NeuroReport</source><volume>16(16)</volume><fpage>1825</fpage><lpage>1828</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16237335</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002389-Hoehl1"><label>27</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hoehl</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Striano</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><year>in press</year><article-title>Neural Processing of Eye Gaze and Threat-Related Emotional Facial Expressions in Infancy.</article-title><source>Child Dev</source></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002389-Woodward1"><label>28</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group pers